{
  "id": "grammar-summary",
  "type": "grammar",
  "level": "B1",
  "title": "Grammar summary",
  "title_es": "Resumen de gramática",
  "icon": "memo",
  "description": "Todas las fórmulas y usos de un vistazo: tiempos verbales, futuro, *should* y *shall*.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formulas",
      "title": "Formulas",
      "title_es": "Fórmulas de todos los tiempos",
      "use": "Cada tiempo con su fórmula en **afirmativa**, **negativa** y **pregunta**. *V* = verbo en infinitivo; *V-ing* = gerundio; *participio* = 3.ª columna de los irregulares (*eaten, been, done*).",
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Presentes",
          "head": [
            "Tiempo",
            "Afirmativa",
            "Negativa",
            "Pregunta",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Present simple",
              "sujeto + **V** (he / she / it + **-s**)",
              "sujeto + **don't / doesn't** + V",
              "**Do / Does** + sujeto + V?",
              "She **works** here. / **Does** she **work** here?"
            ],
            [
              "Present continuous",
              "sujeto + **am / is / are** + **V-ing**",
              "sujeto + **'m not / isn't / aren't** + V-ing",
              "**Am / Is / Are** + sujeto + V-ing?",
              "They'**re cooking**. / **Are** they **cooking**?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Pasado y presente perfecto",
          "head": [
            "Tiempo",
            "Afirmativa",
            "Negativa",
            "Pregunta",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Past simple",
              "sujeto + **V-ed** / irregular",
              "sujeto + **didn't** + V",
              "**Did** + sujeto + V?",
              "I **met** him in 2020. / **Did** you **meet** him?"
            ],
            [
              "Past simple de *be*",
              "sujeto + **was / were**",
              "sujeto + **wasn't / weren't**",
              "**Was / Were** + sujeto…?",
              "Where **were** you yesterday?"
            ],
            [
              "Present perfect simple",
              "sujeto + **have / has** + **participio**",
              "sujeto + **haven't / hasn't** + participio",
              "**Have / Has** + sujeto + participio?",
              "**Have** you ever **eaten** tripe?"
            ],
            [
              "Present perfect continuous",
              "sujeto + **have / has been** + **V-ing**",
              "sujeto + **haven't / hasn't been** + V-ing",
              "**Have / Has** + sujeto + **been** + V-ing?",
              "I'**ve been working** here for 9 years."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Futuro",
          "head": [
            "Forma",
            "Afirmativa",
            "Negativa",
            "Pregunta",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "be going to",
              "sujeto + **am / is / are going to** + V",
              "sujeto + **'m not / isn't / aren't going to** + V",
              "**Am / Is / Are** + sujeto + **going to** + V?",
              "It'**s going to rain**."
            ],
            [
              "will",
              "sujeto + **will ('ll)** + V",
              "sujeto + **won't** + V",
              "**Will** + sujeto + V?",
              "I'**ll help** you."
            ],
            [
              "shall",
              "—",
              "—",
              "**Shall I / we** + V?",
              "**Shall we** eat out?"
            ],
            [
              "Present continuous (futuro)",
              "igual que el presente continuo + expresión de futuro",
              "",
              "",
              "I'**m meeting** Ana **tonight**."
            ],
            [
              "Present simple (futuro)",
              "igual que el presente simple, para horarios",
              "",
              "",
              "The train **leaves** at 6."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Verbos modales: *should*",
          "head": [
            "Forma",
            "Afirmativa",
            "Negativa",
            "Pregunta",
            "Ejemplo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "should",
              "sujeto + **should** + V",
              "sujeto + **shouldn't** + V",
              "**Should** + sujeto + V?",
              "You **should** drink more water."
            ]
          ],
          "note": "Los modales (*should, will, can, must…*) no llevan *-s*, ni *do / does*, ni *to* delante del verbo."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uses",
      "title": "Uses",
      "title_es": "¿Qué tiempo uso? Por usos",
      "use": "Busca **lo que quieres decir** en la primera columna y mira qué tiempo te hace falta.",
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Quiero hablar de…",
          "head": [
            "Quiero hablar de…",
            "Tiempo",
            "Ejemplo",
            "Español"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "hábitos y rutinas",
              "present simple",
              "I **usually have** toast for breakfast.",
              "Normalmente desayuno tostadas."
            ],
            [
              "cosas siempre verdad",
              "present simple",
              "Water **boils** at 100 °C.",
              "El agua hierve a 100 °C."
            ],
            [
              "gustos, opiniones, lo que sé o tengo (verbos de estado)",
              "present simple",
              "I **don't understand** this recipe.",
              "No entiendo esta receta."
            ],
            [
              "algo que pasa ahora mismo",
              "present continuous",
              "She'**s sleeping** now.",
              "Ahora está durmiendo."
            ],
            [
              "algo temporal (estos días)",
              "present continuous",
              "I'**m eating** less meat these days.",
              "Estos días como menos carne."
            ],
            [
              "algo que está cambiando",
              "present continuous",
              "Prices **are going up**.",
              "Los precios están subiendo."
            ],
            [
              "una queja con *always*",
              "present continuous",
              "He'**s always leaving** dirty plates!",
              "¡Siempre deja platos sucios!"
            ],
            [
              "una acción terminada en un momento concreto",
              "past simple",
              "I **met** him five years ago.",
              "Lo conocí hace cinco años."
            ],
            [
              "experiencias en la vida (sin decir cuándo)",
              "present perfect simple",
              "I'**ve never eaten** oysters.",
              "Nunca he comido ostras."
            ],
            [
              "cuánto tiempo llevo haciendo algo",
              "present perfect continuous",
              "I'**ve been learning** English since 2020.",
              "Llevo aprendiendo inglés desde 2020."
            ],
            [
              "un horario futuro",
              "present simple",
              "The museum **opens** at 9.",
              "El museo abre a las 9."
            ],
            [
              "un plan ya organizado",
              "present continuous",
              "I'**m flying** to Rome on Friday.",
              "El viernes vuelo a Roma."
            ],
            [
              "una intención o ambición",
              "be going to",
              "I'**m going to learn** to cook.",
              "Voy a aprender a cocinar."
            ],
            [
              "una predicción con pruebas",
              "be going to",
              "Look at the clouds! It'**s going to rain**.",
              "¡Mira las nubes! Va a llover."
            ],
            [
              "una predicción (mi opinión)",
              "will",
              "I think you'**ll love** it.",
              "Creo que te encantará."
            ],
            [
              "una decisión en el momento",
              "will",
              "I'**ll have** the fish, please.",
              "Tomaré el pescado, por favor."
            ],
            [
              "una promesa u ofrecimiento",
              "will",
              "I **won't tell** anyone.",
              "No se lo diré a nadie."
            ],
            [
              "una sugerencia u ofrecimiento en pregunta",
              "shall",
              "**Shall I** open the window?",
              "¿Abro la ventana?"
            ],
            [
              "un consejo",
              "should",
              "You **should** cut down on sugar.",
              "Deberías tomar menos azúcar."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "time-expressions",
      "title": "Time expressions",
      "title_es": "Expresiones de tiempo por tiempo verbal",
      "use": "Muchas veces la **expresión de tiempo** te da la pista del tiempo verbal. Ojo: con verbos de estado manda el verbo (*I need it **now***, en simple).",
      "tables": [
        {
          "title": "Pistas de tiempo",
          "head": [
            "Tiempo",
            "Expresiones típicas"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Present simple",
              "always, usually, often, sometimes, hardly ever, never, every day, once a week, on Mondays"
            ],
            [
              "Present continuous",
              "now, right now, at the moment, today, this week, these days, nowadays"
            ],
            [
              "Past simple",
              "yesterday, last night / week / year, … ago, in 2019, when I was a child"
            ],
            [
              "Present perfect simple",
              "ever, never, already, yet, just, so far, today (sin terminar)"
            ],
            [
              "Present perfect continuous",
              "How long…?, for + periodo, since + momento"
            ],
            [
              "Futuro",
              "tonight, tomorrow, this weekend, next week, soon, in two days"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "El auxiliar de cada tiempo (para preguntas y negativas)",
          "head": [
            "Tiempo",
            "Auxiliar",
            "Pregunta",
            "Negativa"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Present simple",
              "do / does",
              "**Do** you…? / **Does** she…?",
              "don't / doesn't"
            ],
            [
              "Present continuous",
              "am / is / are",
              "**Are** you …-ing?",
              "'m not / isn't / aren't"
            ],
            [
              "Past simple",
              "did",
              "**Did** you…?",
              "didn't"
            ],
            [
              "Present perfect",
              "have / has",
              "**Have** you…?",
              "haven't / hasn't"
            ],
            [
              "will",
              "will",
              "**Will** you…?",
              "won't"
            ],
            [
              "should",
              "should",
              "**Should** I…?",
              "shouldn't"
            ]
          ],
          "note": "Después de *do, does, did, will, should* el verbo va siempre en **infinitivo sin -s**: *Does she **work**?*, *He didn't **go***."
        }
      ],
      "practice": [
        {
          "q": "I ___ (never / be) to London.",
          "a": "have never been",
          "why": "Experiencia: present perfect."
        },
        {
          "q": "She ___ (work) from home this week.",
          "a": "is working",
          "why": "Temporal: present continuous."
        },
        {
          "q": "We ___ (meet) in 2018.",
          "a": "met",
          "why": "Momento concreto: past simple."
        },
        {
          "q": "How long ___ you ___ (study) English?",
          "a": "have … been studying",
          "why": "Duración hasta ahora."
        },
        {
          "q": "Look! The baby ___ (fall) asleep.",
          "a": "is going to fall",
          "why": "Predicción con pruebas."
        },
        {
          "q": "___ I make some coffee?",
          "a": "Shall",
          "why": "Ofrecimiento con *I*."
        },
        {
          "q": "You ___ (not / drink) so much coffee.",
          "a": "shouldn't drink",
          "why": "Consejo."
        },
        {
          "q": "My brother ___ (not / like) fish.",
          "a": "doesn't like",
          "why": "Verbo de estado: present simple."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
